From 438fc8effdef377374720733be354f0e9a6e4858 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 06:31:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 183/184] zones: Scrolling (scrollable tiling), memory per mode
 and the drag modifier.

- Scrolling (wmake-zones 0.5, wz-scroll): the windows of each output and
  workspace become columns of a strip; opening one adds a column next to
  the active one without changing the others' widths. Columns out of the
  view are parked beyond every output, so nothing shows on a neighbour.
  Activating a parked window scrolls to it. Commands scroll/column; focus,
  swap, grow and shrink act on the strip; dropping a window reorders the
  columns, resizing it sets the column width.
- Memory of the free mode: entering the tiling or the scrolling keeps
  each window's box, zone and maximization; back to Zones or off, each one
  returns as it was (before, a snapped window lost its zone).
- A window dragged out of the zones keeps the size the user gave it and
  leaves its zone (RestoreSizeOnUnsnap now defaults to false).
- The drag modifier of the configuration (DragModifier, Ctrl+Alt) on every
  window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
